@allow(star_import) # reason: deduplication facade, re-exports the single runner implementation
# =========================================================================
# Test Runner Main — DEDUPLICATION FACADE
# =========================================================================
#
# This file used to be a SECOND, divergent copy of the test runner. It is now
# a thin re-export of the single implementation:
#
#     src/app/test_runner_new/test_runner_main.spl
#
# Why: two copies existed and had drifted. The app copy was ahead on ten
# behaviours (--test-json-worker mode, --no-cache daemon-cache bypass,
# TRESP_CACHED failure diagnostics, arg validation, .md target routing, test
# database persistence + test_result.md generation, spipe docgen, worker cap,
# test_daemon_ensure_responsive, spl-doctest reporting) while this copy was
# ahead on ONE (the --timeout -> session_startup_timeout_ms floor). Neither was
# a superset. The lone lib-only behaviour has been ported into the app copy, so
# nothing is lost by pointing here.
#
# Liveness proof: instrumenting both entry functions and running
# `bin/simple test test/01_unit/io` printed the app-copy probe and never the
# lib-copy probe. `bin/simple test` reaches this code via
# src/app/cli/_CliMain/main_and_help.spl -> app.test_runner_new.test_runner_main
# .run_test_cli. The `main` below is kept only so the
# std.*.test_runner barrels and std.test_runner.main keep resolving.
#
# DO NOT re-add an implementation here. Fix the app copy instead.

export use app.test_runner_new.test_runner_main.*

use app.test_runner_new.test_runner_main.{run_test_cli}

fn main() -> i64:
    run_test_cli()
